{"case_id":"C036","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":98,"change_types":["internal bug fix","bit-reader state normalization","debug invariant checks"],"affected_functions":["BrotliBitReaderNormalize","BrotliBitReaderUnload","BrotliJumpToByteBoundary","BrotliDropBytes","BrotliCopyBytes"],"reason":"The commit changes only internal bit-reader accumulator cleanup and invariants. It adds no decoder entry point, configuration, initialization requirement, API protocol, or input constraint. The existing harness already invokes BrotliDecoderDecompressStream with attacker-controlled input and varies delivery between whole-input and 1–7-byte chunks, so it continues to exercise the relevant decoding and input-discontinuity paths without modification.","evidence":["The public call used by the harness, BrotliDecoderDecompressStream, is unchanged.","BrotliBitReaderNormalize is an internal helper that masks stale bits in br->val_; it introduces no harness-visible parameter or setup requirement.","BrotliBitReaderUnload, BrotliJumpToByteBoundary, and BrotliCopyBytes now normalize existing state, while BrotliDropBytes only adds BROTLI_DCHECK assertions for an existing internal precondition.","The harness selects addend == size or addend <= 7 and repeatedly supplies chunks through the same decoder state, already covering both fast and incremental decoding paths relevant to bit-reader unloading and discontinuous input."],"recommended_action":"Keep the existing fuzz harness unchanged; no maintenance is required for this internal state-correctness change."}
